[{:db/id -1
 :adr/id "adr-2609071100-capacity-that-folds-prefill-into-throughput"
 :adr/title "A capacity number that divides completion tokens by wall clock is measuring the prompt, not the fleet"
 :adr/status "accepted"
 :adr/date "2026-09-07"
 :adr/body "## Context\n\n`https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/models` published, for `murakumo-main`\n(Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M), `capacity.text[output].value = 60` tokens per minute,\n`max_concurrency = 2`, and `capacity-measured-aggregate-tok-s = 1.04` at\nconcurrency 1, measured 2026-09-05. The accompanying `capacity-method` recorded\na thirty-five-fold degradation from 35.56 tok/s at concurrency 4 six days\nearlier, named \"b70 head queueing server-side\" as the cause, and said it was\nflagged for the operator rather than papered over\n(`network-awai/cloud-murakumo-api` commit 61c1d8b).\n\nMeasured 2026-09-07 on the b70 head itself rather than through the public\nboundary, over every completed task in a 24-hour window:\n\n- decode 20.2-20.9 ms per token, i.e. 47.8-49.4 tokens/second\n- prompt eval 975-1,220 tokens/second\n- host load average 0.35, llama-server active, `/health` ok\n\nThe head is not degraded. One task in that window spent 13,275 ms evaluating a\n12,951-token prompt before its first byte, with `n_prompt_tokens_cache: 0`.\n\n## Finding\n\nThe published figure is `sum(usage.completion_tokens) / wall_clock`, and the\nwall clock includes prefill. Sixteen output tokens behind a 13-second uncached\nprefill publish as about 1.2 tok/s while the GPU decodes at 48. The number is\ntherefore dominated by prompt length and prompt-cache state, not by serving\ncapacity, and **two such numbers are not comparable to each other** unless the\nprompt was the same. 08-31's 35.56 and 09-05's 1.04 were not.\n\nThe concurrency-2 timeouts have a separate and ordinary cause: the unit\n`murakumo-b70-llama.service` runs `--parallel 1`, one slot, so a second\nconcurrent request waits for the first, and a first request taking ~25 s pushes\nthe second past the edge timeout. The published `max_concurrency` of 2 is twice\nthe real slot count.\n\nSo one published value folds three independent facts together -- decode rate,\nprefill cost, and queueing behind a single slot -- and a prompt-cache miss\nreads as a fleet collapse. This is ADR-2608136000's shape at the level of a\npublic capacity declaration: a measurement that cannot distinguish two\nsituations returns the same value for both.\n\nNotably the honest instinct made it worse. The 09-05 commit deliberately\npublished the unflattering number rather than hiding it, and that is right; but\nan unexamined bad number published humbly is still an unexamined bad number,\nand it understated the owner's own fleet by roughly 45x for two days.\n\n## Decision\n\nA capacity declaration must publish decode rate and prefill rate as distinct\nvalues, with a concurrency figure that matches the real slot count, and must\nsay where each was taken -- server-side `llama-server` timings and end-to-end\nmeasurements through the public boundary answer different questions. Both are\nlegitimate; publishing one under the other's name is not. Any aggregate that\nmixes phases must be labelled prompt-length-dependent so nobody compares two of\nthem.\n\n## Status of the work\n\nRecorded, not yet fixed. The re-cut declaration, the gad and xavier\nmeasurements needed to pick pool-wide numbers, and the diagnosis of the zero\nprompt-cache hits are the standing backlog of the Hermes profile\n`murakumo-infer-maturity` (cron job 9ea532317c62, every 4h, workdir this\nsuperproject). The public blog post at\n`https://murakumo.cloud/blog/2026-murakumo-vs-vllm-sglang-llamacpp` already\nstates the correction, so the published page and the published API disagree\nuntil item 1 of that backlog lands -- deliberately, because the page's whole\nargument is that the operator publishes its own unflattering measurements.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```\nssh jun@100.119.10.43 'journalctl -u murakumo-b70-llama.service --no-pager \\\n  --since \"-24 hours\" | grep -E \"eval time =\"'\ncurl -s https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/models\n```\n\nDo not copy today's numbers forward. Run the commands."}]
